;; Recorded circular dependencies between modules. This file only ever shrinks.
;; metabase.core.module-cycles-test fails when the tree drifts past it; `./bin/mage
;; fix-module-cycles` tightens it to match, and local test runs do that automatically.
;;
;; Two graphs are recorded:
;;   :uses               -- the `require` graph, from the :uses sets in the modules config.
;;   :uses+model-imports -- the same, plus an edge to whichever module exports each
;;                          :model/X a module imports. Those resolve through Toucan's
;;                          registry rather than a `require`, so :uses cannot see them --
;;                          but the model's namespace still has to load first, which makes
;;                          them real dependencies for loading a module on its own.
;;
;; Within each graph, :sccs holds every strongly connected component -- a set of modules
;; that can all reach each other -- and :edges is how many dependencies run between members.
;; A module may not join an SCC, two SCCs may not merge, and a new SCC may not appear.
;; Splitting an SCC or dropping out of one is the whole point and always passes.
;;
;; :unconstrained-modules -- modules whose dependencies the config does not record:
;; `:uses :any` hides requires, `:model-imports :bypass` hides model references. Cycles
;; routed through them are invisible here, so neither set may grow.
